{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41161624",
      "title": "Linking & Navigating",
      "lectureOrder": 42,
      "videoOrder": 40,
      "sourceHash": "f9ebe2ef662c1468fba654ef92e351eebd235bf1c0bc89f8efcb7fe6690d251f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.66,
          "en": "So how can we make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.66,
          "end": 7.44,
          "en": "that clicking new post opens this new post modal?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.44,
          "end": 10.02,
          "en": "Well, we need to create a link between these two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.02,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "different routes in the end, and for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 14.91,
          "en": "we can go to the MainHeader component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.91,
          "end": 16.59,
          "en": "which is where I have this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.59,
          "end": 19.8,
          "en": "and we now must edit this component a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.8,
          "end": 22.35,
          "en": "We must replace this button with a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.35,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "to this /create-post route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 27.5,
          "en": "That's in the end what we want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.397,
          "end": 31.14,
          "en": "So for that, we could replace button with an anchor element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.14,
          "end": 34.05,
          "en": "which is the right element for creating a link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.05,
          "end": 36.24,
          "en": "and get rid of the on click handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "and get rid of that prop, which we don't support anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 42.93,
          "en": "and instead, add the ref attribute here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.93,
          "end": 45.093,
          "en": "and point at create-post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.006,
          "end": 49.5,
          "en": "If we do that and save this, the styling's a bit off,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "we get this underline effect, but we can ignore that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 55.362,
          "en": "If I click this, it seems to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.362,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "but I say it seems to work because actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "if you watch this refresh icon, if I click new post,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 65.01,
          "en": "you see it briefly change to a cross,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.01,
          "end": 68.52,
          "en": "which means that technically a brand new request was sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.52,
          "end": 70.62,
          "en": "to the server serving this React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.62,
          "end": 74.22,
          "en": "and we technically downloaded the entire React app again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 78.12,
          "en": "and started it as a new instance of that app, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.12,
          "end": 82.1,
          "en": "so it's just as if I manually pressed this refresh button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.1,
          "end": 85.32,
          "en": "This works, but it means that we leave the single page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.32,
          "end": 87.99,
          "en": "application just to load it again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.99,
          "end": 90.687,
          "en": "which means any global state would be lost,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.687,
          "end": 93.39,
          "en": "and we, of course, also unnecessarily download",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.39,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "and execute all the JavaScript code again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 97.893,
          "en": "which is not great for performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.78999999999999,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "For that reason, we want to stay in that single application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 104.4,
          "en": "world and just make sure that the URL changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.4,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "and a new component gets loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 108.75,
          "en": "without sending a new request to the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.75,
          "end": 110.223,
          "en": "serving the React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 113.88,
          "en": "And this is, of course, a common use case, and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.88,
          "end": 118.88,
          "en": "we can import the link component from react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.19,
          "end": 121.02,
          "en": "We should use this link component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.02,
          "end": 123.15,
          "en": "instead of the anchor element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.15,
          "end": 125.7,
          "en": "Under the hood, this renders an anchor element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.7,
          "end": 129.852,
          "en": "but it prevents the browser's default of sending a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.852,
          "end": 133.14,
          "en": "This link component doesn't take the ref attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.14,
          "end": 136.23,
          "en": "but instead the to property, but we can and should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.23,
          "end": 138.243,
          "en": "then still target create-post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "I'll also now briefly go to my main header module CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "and they are on button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 149.22,
          "en": "I'll simply set text decoration to non",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.22,
          "end": 150.78300000000002,
          "en": "to get rid of the underlining.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 154.98,
          "en": "But the more important part is the usage of link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 159.51,
          "en": "With that, if we save this and we go back to /nothing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.51,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "and I click new post, you now see it did not reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 165.99,
          "en": "the page, and you can also tell that it didn't do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.99,
          "end": 170.13,
          "en": "by the fact that if I load this, you have this list of posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.13,
          "end": 172.23,
          "en": "and if I click here, you see in the background,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.23,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "it's not re-fetched again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 176.85,
          "en": "Instead, we're still on the same single page application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.85,
          "end": 179.85,
          "en": "and that's, of course, the user experience we want to offer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.85,
          "end": 182.883,
          "en": "It's way better than the other experience we had before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.11,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "Of course, we now also want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 188.88,
          "en": "that we close this modal if we click the backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.88,
          "end": 191.28,
          "en": "or if we click the cancel button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.28,
          "end": 193.47,
          "en": "Also if we submit it, but submitting this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.47,
          "end": 196.443,
          "en": "and handing submission is something we'll handle later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 200.46,
          "en": "Now, to also navigate when we click the backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.46,
          "end": 203.49,
          "en": "of the modal, we can go to the modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.49,
          "end": 206.76,
          "en": "and there we can get rid of that onClose prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.76,
          "end": 208.8,
          "en": "because we can actually handle clicks inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.8,
          "end": 212.31,
          "en": "of that modal component now, assuming that we always use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.31,
          "end": 215.37,
          "en": "this modal to wrap a page with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.37,
          "end": 217.82999999999998,
          "en": "so, to use it as a wrapper inside of a route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.82999999999998,
          "end": 220.65,
          "en": "and that we always want to go back to another route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.65,
          "end": 222.513,
          "en": "if we click on the backdrop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.62,
          "end": 226.56,
          "en": "But if that is our assumption, we can add a function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.56,
          "end": 231.56,
          "en": "the closeHandler, which will be assigned to this onClick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.84,
          "end": 234.243,
          "en": "event listener on this backdrop diff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.14,
          "end": 237.66,
          "en": "And in there, I now also want to navigate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.66,
          "end": 240.69,
          "en": "but now we have to navigate programmatically here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.69,
          "end": 244.2,
          "en": "because this is now not a link, but instead an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.2,
          "end": 246.123,
          "en": "that's executed when we click a diff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.96,
          "end": 249.42,
          "en": "We could replace the diff with a link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249.42,
          "end": 252.12,
          "en": "but here I'll stick to a diff also to show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 252.12,
          "end": 254.7,
          "en": "how programmatic navigation works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.7,
          "end": 257.43,
          "en": "because sometimes you must initiate navigation actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 260.073,
          "en": "from inside code and this is how you can do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 260.91,
          "end": 265.05,
          "en": "You can import another feature, another function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 265.05,
          "end": 268.44,
          "en": "from react-router-dom for that, and that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 271.443,
          "en": "is actually a hook, the useNavigate hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 272.49,
          "end": 275.31,
          "en": "a hook provided by react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.31,
          "end": 277.17,
          "en": "In React, you don't just have the hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 277.17,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "that are built into React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 280.62,
          "en": "Instead, you can also create your own hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.62,
          "end": 283.08,
          "en": "and you learn how to do that in my course as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 283.08,
          "end": 286.71,
          "en": "and therefore third party packages like react-router-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.71,
          "end": 289.053,
          "en": "also can create and share hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.61,
          "end": 293.64,
          "en": "Now, useNavigate can be executed to get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 293.64,
          "end": 296.97,
          "en": "of a navigate function, which I store in a constant here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 296.97,
          "end": 298.971,
          "en": "but this one yet holds a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.971,
          "end": 301.62,
          "en": "Therefore, we can execute it as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.62,
          "end": 305.67,
          "en": "here in closeHandler, and then we pass the path to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 305.67,
          "end": 309.3,
          "en": "to which we want to navigate when it's executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 309.3,
          "end": 312.33,
          "en": "And we could navigate to /nothing to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312.33,
          "end": 314.37,
          "en": "that if I click on the backdrop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.37,
          "end": 316.563,
          "en": "I navigate back to the starting page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.88,
          "end": 320.22,
          "en": "We could also make this more flexible and use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.22,
          "end": 323.322,
          "en": "a relative path and use two dots here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 323.322,
          "end": 326.79,
          "en": "which works in the same way as two dots work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 326.79,
          "end": 329.43,
          "en": "in the terminal when using the CD command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 329.43,
          "end": 332.1,
          "en": "You go up one level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 332.1,
          "end": 333.87,
          "en": "It's the same here for routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 333.87,
          "end": 338.25,
          "en": "You can use this special relative path here to go up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 338.25,
          "end": 341.85,
          "en": "to the parent route, so to the route above this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 341.85,
          "end": 343.11,
          "en": "that's currently active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 343.11,
          "end": 345.54,
          "en": "This would make the modal a bit more dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 345.54,
          "end": 346.86,
          "en": "It's up to you what you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 346.86,
          "end": 349.26,
          "en": "Here I'll use this approach, and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 349.26,
          "end": 352.5,
          "en": "if this is loaded as part of the /create-post route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 352.5,
          "end": 354.65999999999997,
          "en": "we would go up to the parent route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 354.65999999999997,
          "end": 357.033,
          "en": "which is this slash route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 358.05,
          "end": 360.3,
          "en": "So therefore, now with that, if I save this all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 360.3,
          "end": 363.51,
          "en": "we can still open and close the modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 363.51,
          "end": 366,
          "en": "We can also make sure that the cancel button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 366,
          "end": 367.83,
          "en": "closes the modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 367.83,
          "end": 370.53,
          "en": "for this, we can go to the NewPost component again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 370.53,
          "end": 373.02,
          "en": "which is where we have this cancel button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 373.02,
          "end": 375.57,
          "en": "and we could now also initiate programmatic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 375.57,
          "end": 378.09,
          "en": "navigation here again, but here in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 378.09,
          "end": 381.12,
          "en": "it makes more sense to render a link again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 381.12,
          "end": 385.17,
          "en": "Therefore, we can again import the link component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 385.17,
          "end": 390.12,
